{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011ePUrNHsU3XRn2PJSDsRnF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user personal productivity system built for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (no syncing, no external siblings). Grounded claims about what it is and ships:\n\n- **A markdown-backed task/project manager.** The source of truth is plain markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, `CANCELLED.md`, `SAVED_FOR_LATER.md`). Tasks move through a lifecycle â€” active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved-for-later â†’ restored â€” and every change is logged to `logs/YYYY-MM-DD.md`.\n\n- **Two interfaces over the same data.** `anchor_gui.py` is the primary app â€” a stdlib-only Python HTTP server that renders a fully interactive browser dashboard at `http://localhost:8777` and writes directly to the markdown. `anchor.py` mirrors that logic as a CLI and regenerates the static `dashboard.html`. It runs persistently as the Windows NSSM service **`anchor`** on host `PUTER`/`gwl-server`.\n\n- **A self-test safety net.** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs daily at 5 AM via Task Scheduler â€” it parses every markdown file, boots a throwaway server, exercises every endpoint and state transition, walks the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed, and writes `health_reports/YYYY-MM-DD.md` (red banner on failure).\n\n- **An evolving \"R&D control surface\" for trio-driven development.** Layered over the task manager is a per-project cockpit that manages work done by the skill trio **researchPrime (research) â†’ Crucible (planning) â†’ Foreman (build)**. It models each trio run as a *session*, generates cached/validated summaries, and tracks ideas (\"Grass Catchers\"), deliverables, and effort (tokens/cost/time).\n\n- **Shipped in four versioned waves of that surface:** v2 (session model, cached summaries, grass lane, interactive REPL terminal), v3 \"Mission Control\" (real **ConPTY** terminals via the one allowed native dep `pywinpty`, per-session git-worktree isolation, a stacking window manager, in-place summaries, Ghost World Labs branding), and v4 \"Project Cockpit\" (the current default â€” lane tiles with status lights, inline expanding panels stacking a summary over a resizable xterm.js terminal, a Claudeâ†”Gemini engine toggle, per-lane doc roles, project cost rollups, grass-promote, and type-aware deliverable launch). v4 is **built (9 waves GREEN) and merged to master**.\n\n- **Stdlib-only by rule, with one declared exception** (`pywinpty`, lazy, terminal-only), enforced by `distro.py`'s import scan; all files stay plain-text and CLI-accessible.\n\nThe current branch (`foreman/rnd-v4.1-cockpit`) appears to be iterating on the v4 cockpit (project-window rendering as the Paradigm-2 tile layout, version-stamped project windows)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45330,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3482944f-03dc-4902-a0f9-612b5e93197f","uuid":"1c937778-fa4c-4e49-9f45-5abe02b11082","request_id":"req_011Cc1vvCQxSX8Gc6BKdP5PC"}
